《墨龙借雨》 The Ink Dragon Borrows the Rain — a Chinese ink-wash film, 132 s

All imagery is generated by code in this folder (a Canvas2D brush engine and a WebGL rice-paper compositor). No photos, no AI-generated images.
Story, characters, calligraphy strokes, seal design, Foley and music are original.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence files in node_modules/@fontsource/*/LICENSE, installed from npm by build.sh):
- Ma Shan Zheng (马善政毛笔楷书) — Ma Shan Zheng, via @fontsource/ma-shan-zheng. Inscriptions, the colophon and the seven subtitle lines; for the title
  墨龙借雨 its glyphs are used only as a skeleton (stroke centrelines snapped to the glyph's medial axis, written by the brush engine).
- Noto Serif SC — Google, via @fontsource/noto-serif-sc. Labels on the model sheet and test pages only; not in the film.

Music (original score, music/score.py):
- Guqin: physical-model plucked string, core/audio/pluck.py (synthesis, no samples).
- Xiao (substitute: sampled flute, low-passed, with breath noise), bass drum, gran cassa, timpani, frame drum, woodblock, claves, small gong, tam-tam:
  Samples (CC0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios), Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios).

Sound effects: synthesised in mix.py with core/audio/sfx.py (no recordings).

Brush engine (ink.js) and rice-paper compositor (comp.js) copied from the Lemo-Opuscar library's Chinese Ink Wash style (styles/ink-wash/demo), with
land.js (mountains, cun, pines, ripples); the library is under its own LICENSE. Everything else in this folder was written for this film.
